  "interpretation": "Domain composition differs significantly between high- and low-BCS batches (chi2=230.74, p<0.001, df=5). High-BCS batches concentrate on science/taxonomy and event/temporal domains (relations like follows/followed_by, part_of/has_part, member_of, instance_of), while low-BCS batches spread across geography and creative_work domains (country_of_citizenship, composer, original_language_of_film_or_TV_show). However, this domain concentration is an expected property of embedding-based BCS: types within the same domain naturally share more semantic features, yielding higher pairwise cosine similarity. Domain composition is thus a mediator of the BCS\u2013performance relationship, not an independent confound.",
